+def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
+    """
+    Recolor grey objects by matching their enclosed hole shapes to a left-edge template legend.
+
+    Input structure:
+    - The background is Black, and a vertical stack of small legend blocks touches the left edge.
+    - Each legend block is a colored 5x5 frame whose 3x3 interior contains a Black-backed template shape in the frame color.
+    - The main area contains 4-connected Grey foreground objects, each enclosing one or more Black holes.
+
+    Rule:
+    - Read every left-edge legend frame and store the 3x3 interior non-Black pixels as a template mask keyed by shape up to rotation and flip.
+    - For each Grey object, extract all enclosed Black hole components and match each normalized hole shape to a legend template.
